WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.000
AI can write Ren'Py code.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.267
But after every change, it still has to guess
what the player actually sees.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.400
RenForge closes that blind loop.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.133
It maps the project, launches the real game,
and reads its live state —

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.833
screens, variables, choices, errors, and pixels.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.067
Agents can advance, hover, click, type, save and reload,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.200
validating every interaction
against the current frame.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.500
They can inspect the scene tree, measure layouts,
and detect overlaps —

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.500
compare screenshots and verify contrast
before calling the work done.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.900
Then RenForge can explore branches,
audit assets and translations,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.500
run complete scenarios, diagnose failures,
and build distributions.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.200
MCP. CLI. Dashboard. A live Ren'Py bridge.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.067
One real feedback loop.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.200
RenForge is open source.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.800
Build Ren'Py with sight.
